#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Mansur 2024 postprocessed AC clock baseline, with retained legacy replay.

Run: python offline_multi_gnss_combine_causal_balanced.py CONFIG.json
Check equations: python offline_multi_gnss_combine_causal_balanced.py --self-test
Inspect a failed run: python offline_multi_gnss_combine_causal_balanced.py --diagnose PATH_TO_quality.json
Replay saved moments: python offline_multi_gnss_combine_causal_balanced.py --replay-vce PATH_TO_quality.json
Dependency: NumPy. Delivered config selects pipeline=mansur2024, 300 s sampling.
Delivered config uses unconstrained LS-VCE as the paper baseline.
Set vce_constraint=nonnegative only for the explicitly labelled extension
from Teunissen-Amiri-Simkooei2008 Sect3.6, not for an unmodified replication.
No B2B, Huber, satellite/epoch quality multipliers, rolling calibration, variance
floor, weight-ratio clipping, or silent equal-weight fallback in the baseline.
CLK AS values are seconds; SP3 positions are km and clocks microseconds.
Full-day data are used, including future epochs. This is not a real-time replay.
COD REF is only evaluated after AC preprocessing/estimation. At least three ACs
and adequate common core samples are required in each constellation.
The exact reduced LSVCE normal equations follow Mansur2022 Eqs15,22,23, used by
Mansur2024 Eqs15-18. Underdocumented numerical choices are in config/quality.json.
Supplying combined_orbit_file uses an existing combined orbit; otherwise the
separate supporting orbit module fits AC-wise Helmert parameters and estimates
orbit variances. No original-day numerical results or PPP performance are claimed.
For retained experimental functions select pipeline=legacy_causal explicitly.
"""
